00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:49.000
But this is what makes personal agents very dangerous. And so the lethal trifecta, it applies to more than just second brains or personal agents. This applies to all agents.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:11:05.000
There are three parts to the trifecta here. Obviously, that's why it's called a trifecta. We have private data access, we have untrusted content, so there are other people that are able to give inputs into our agent. And then we have what is called an exfiltration vector.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:19.000
And exfiltration vector, it's kind of a fancy phrase. All it means is there's some way for the agent to send information back to a malicious attacker through, you know, making an API request or sending a message on Telegram, something like that.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:30.000
The thought process behind the lethal trifecta is your agent is at most risk of being compromised if it meets all three of these criteria.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:50.000
So if it can access private data, receive untrusted inputs, and have some way to send information back out. Because think about it this way. If your AI agent is able to access things in your email, you know, access private data, and it can receive incoming emails, so theoretically there could be a prompt injection attack that comes in through an email.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:12:13.000
But if there's no way for it to send private data back out to the attacker, your agent is a lot harder to compromise. If it only matches two out of the three criteria in the lethal trifecta. And just to give you another example here, let's say that there is an exfiltration vector. Your agent is allowed to make arbitrary API requests so it can send data out to the internet, and it could theoretically have a prompt injection attack.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:30.000
But there's no access to private data, then it doesn't really matter if there is a prompt injection attack, because what is it really going to access, even if it could send something to an attacker? Not that your agent is fully secure at this point, but just saying that, like, we really need to hit on all three of these points.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.000
In order for there to really be a big, big security concern with our agent.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:44.000
And the thing is, in order for a second brain to be useful for us, it really has to have all three of these criteria met by default.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:13:00.000
